In article <265vpbINN2m28@rs1.rrz.Uni-Koeln.DE> aeg03@rrz.uni-koeln.de (Jan T. Kim) writes:

| My question is, how can I break free from an electric eel? I invariably
| got the message "You cannot escape from the electric eel", no matter
| what I tried to do.

The other day my super wizard (boots of speed, amulet of reflection,
Mjollnir, max luck, lots of HP etc.) died from the same cause (well,
he actually drowned since the eel managed to pull him down into the
water, sob, sob).  This made me think about how it could have been
avoided.  I obviously haven't tried it, but next time I definitely
will.

1) Kill the eel before he kills you.  Don't use Mjollnir as I did
since I think that electric eels have shock resistance.

2) Engrave 'Elbereth'.  Use an athame if you've got one.  Wands of
digging/fire/lightning should also do and some gems.  Otherwise any
weapon you can throw away afterwards, but write the text in two parts:
start with 'Elbe' and then add to the engraving 'reth'.  I haven't
tried this so maybe you should make some experiments before you
approach the eel next time.

The 'Elbereth' trick works with mimics and owlbears so it should work
with eels.

3) Maybe you can pray to your god.  If he will cure you from blindness
he should also cure you from being held by an eel, but I don't know
for sure.

4) Confuse the eel by throwing a potion or blind it by using a camera.
Don't know if it'll help though.

Damn those eels.   ;^|
